{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אל תרגזו", :translit "al tirgezu", :gloss "do not be agitated"} {:he "אל תסכמו עלי לומר אחינו גדול הארץ לעשות עול לשום אדם", :translit "al taskimu alai l'omar akhenu gadol ha'aretz la'asot ol l'shum adam", :gloss "do not conspire against me to say our brother is great in the land to do wrong to anyone"} {:he "אלא אל תרגזו לשום אדם לילך בדרך על שדה זרועה", :translit "ela al tirgezu l'shum adam lalechet b'derekh al sadeh z'ru'ah", :gloss "rather do not be agitated against anyone to walk on the road through a sown field"} {:he "ד\"א אמר להם אל תתעסקו בדבר הלכה", :translit "d\"a amar lahem al tit'ask'u b'dvar halakhah", :gloss "another interpretation he said to them do not engage in matters of halakhah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Three readings of 'al tirgezu': (1) do not conspire to use Joseph's power against others; (2) do not provoke anyone by walking through sown fields; (3) do not engage in halakhic discourse while traveling."}], :frame {:text "Genesis 45:24 records Joseph telling his brothers 'al tirgezu ba'derekh' as they depart Egypt. Genesis Rabbah 100:2 interprets the phrase as a warning not to engage in halakhic dispute on the road, and alternatively as a prohibition against entering sown fields. The Talmud connects 'tirgezu' to quarreling, reading Joseph's admonition as a charge against causing harm or conflict.", :sources ["Genesis Rabbah 100:2" "Genesis 45:24"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אליהם אל תרגזו", :translit "aleihem al tirgezu", :gloss "to them do not be agitated"} {:he "אל תדברו בהלכה", :translit "al tidb'ru b'halakhah", :gloss "do not speak of halakhah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אליהם אל תרגזו", :b "אל תדברו בהלכה"}], :frame {:text "Genesis Rabbah 100:2 records the interpretation that Joseph's instruction 'al tirgezu ba'derekh' (Genesis 45:24) means the brothers should not engage in halakhic discourse on the road. Ba'al HaTurim encodes this midrashic reading as a gematria equivalence between the phrase 'aleihem al tirgezu' and 'al tidberu b'halakhah.'", :sources ["Genesis Rabbah 100:2" "Genesis 45:24"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אלהם אל תרגזו בדרך", :translit "elahem al tirgezu b'derekh", :gloss "to them do not be agitated on the road"} {:he "אל תפסעו פסיעה גסה", :translit "al tif's'u p'si'ah gasah", :gloss "do not take a wide step"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אלהם אל תרגזו בדרך", :b "אל תפסעו פסיעה גסה"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that one may not take wide steps (pesi'ah gasah) except when descending, as R. Yochanan linked the practice to arrogance (Berakhot 43b). The Yerushalmi records that one who walks with wide steps loses one five-hundredth of his eyesight (Yerushalmi Berakhot 8:5). Ba'al HaTurim ties this prohibition to Joseph's travel warning in Genesis 45:24 through a gematria of 'elahem al tirgezu b'derekh.'", :sources ["Berakhot 43b" "Yerushalmi Berakhot 8:5" "Genesis 45:24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Three readings of 'al tirgezu': (1) do not conspire to use Joseph's power against others; (2) do not provoke anyone by walking through sown fields; (3) do not engage in halakhic discourse while traveling.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "אליהם אל תרגזו", :a-value 733, :b "אל תדברו בהלכה", :b-value 705, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "אלהם אל תרגזו בדרך", :a-value 949, :b "אל תפסעו פסיעה גסה", :b-value 940, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:11:51.147029173Z", :model "glm-5.2"}